  "summary": [
    "FR-006 defines task-related document search that prioritizes avoiding misses over precision",
    "Search uses the ToC for the given key, or the reserved key all in standalone mode",
    "Missing ToC returns a first-build-needed response; existing ToC is inspected for rebuild necessity",
    "When rebuild is needed the user chooses rebuild-then-search or search the existing ToC",
    "Two-choice prompt is skipped when AI-generated fields are missing or stale (REQ-006 FR-022)",
    "A target specification file records the checked key and Index target spec so rebuild covers the same targets",
    "Rebuild-scale counts go to stdout and per-document details go to a work file",
    "Undeterminable rebuild necessity stops the search as a fault without offering the existing ToC",
    "Search results include document ID, ToC path, reason, sections, and ToC state",
    "AC-019 acceptance criterion for the pre-search ToC rebuild confirmation"
  ],
